  "checkbox component" here means plain HTML + a bit of vanilla JS.

  One thing genuinely changes the deliverable, so I'll ask before designing.

  [1mThe fork:[0m whether the page gets [3mone[0m checkbox, or a checkbox [3mper task[0m in a list. The page currently has no tasks in it
  at all, so "mark items as done" doesn't yet have items to attach to.

  - [1mSingle checkbox[0m — one labeled checkbox in [38;5;153m<main>[39m with on/off state. Smallest possible change, matches "nothing
    fancy" literally. Costs: doesn't actually mark anything; you'd extend it later.
  - [1mCheckbox per task, hardcoded list[0m — a few placeholder task items, each with its own checkbox and a done/not-done
    state. Buys you the real "mark items as done" behavior. Costs: I invent placeholder task text, and it implies a
    task-data shape you may want to decide differently later.

  Neither is expensive to change afterward — it's one file with no consumers. I lean toward the per-task list, because
  "mark items as done" only means something with items, and a lone checkbox marks nothing.

